# Deployment Safety

## Context

Every deployment freezes a reviewed configuration and exact base/target SHA. A database reservation, shared environment lock, atomic claim and execution token protect against concurrent workers.

## Decisions

- Compare/hash configuration with recursively canonical JSON object keys while preserving list order and scalar types. Cached review preflight is permitted for 120 seconds only with matching configuration and current inspection format; explicit refresh, recovery and worker checks remain fresh. Batched inspection must retain bounded output, each exit code and fail closed on incomplete/malformed frames.
- Trace preview, confirmation, enqueue, execution, cancellation and reconciliation before changing a state or candidate field. Update digest validation and worker checks with any new candidate metadata; do not mutate saved candidates.
- Require a canonical root, exact registered origin and branch, successful fetch, fast-forward ancestry and unchanged reviewed base/target. Local changes do not automatically block deployment; preserve Git overwrite checks. Enabled Pre hooks require a frozen worktree/index/untracked content digest; verify it before hooks and recheck unchanged base/target afterward. Hard reset is an explicit, initially disabled typed option. Never substitute the latest origin SHA at execution time.
- Preserve typed built-in commands, POSIX quoting, disabled automatic Git hooks and merge overwrite protection for ignored files. User-authorized custom Shell hooks are administrator-configured, independently enabled, ordered by Pre/Post phase and frozen in review. They may explicitly run cleanup, migrations or other maintenance; never execute them during preview or silently enable them. Keep normal requester confirmation, grants, ownership, timeouts and output sanitization around every hook.
- Recovery is a new reviewed candidate linked to a failed deployment whose code was updated. It requires fresh preflight with HEAD and fetched origin at the failed target, fresh grants/MFA, current configuration and fresh requester confirmation.
- Recovery skips the Git merge and reruns all selected pipeline steps and enabled hooks. Show that replay explicitly; do not silently resume uncertain steps or offer recovery for unknown state without reconciliation.
- Recheck requester deployment grants, digest, expiry and configuration before execution and each step. Independent approval is retired for all targets, including production. Legacy awaiting_approval requests require explicit reconfirmation by the original requester; never auto-enqueue them or rewrite saved candidate metadata. Retain legacy approval fields only for digest/fingerprint compatibility and audit history.
- Keep reservation plus job creation atomic and enforce execution ownership when changing worker state. Duplicated jobs must not quarantine another worker's execution.
- Single-time schedules freeze their UTC instant and display timezone in candidate integrity. Require requester confirmation before the due time; future plans do not reserve targets. Due dispatch uses the shared environment lock, fresh grants/MFA/configuration and atomic reservation plus database enqueue. Workers reject early execution and recheck the exact repository. Expire after the bounded execution window; never auto-select newer commits or bypass unknown quarantine.
- Choosing a time on the existing review pins the same base/target, preflight and scripts into a new immutable candidate without SSH. Validate the source digest, expiry and current authorization/configuration; atomically cancel the source and confirm the replacement under environment/source locks. Identical retries return the same plan, conflicting times fail, and requester confirmation binds the new digest.
- Preserve partial results on known failure. Connection loss, timeouts, unexpected faults and final HEAD mismatch require unknown-state quarantine. Release quarantine only after an administrator's attestation and repository inspection.
- Buffer bounded whole-command output and redact known secrets before persistence. A selected health check requires verified HTTPS and a 2xx result without redirects.

## Verification

- Exercise normal success, partial failure/recovery, production confirmation without approval, legacy requester reconfirmation, permission/configuration revocation, cancellation, stale SHA, duplicate execution and unknown-state quarantine for changes to this flow.
- Use real local Git tests for Git semantics and separate-worker tests for ownership changes; keep their fixture roots guarded and isolated from live data.
